{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 8b39bee2 (S1-F), 6eacd6ac (NF-4) and Q-D1 of e8a58e69.\n\nS1-F. Run its gate now. The cutover lane edits source for those\nminutes and runs nothing. A small head lands while the cutover\nhead is not at its gate. When the cutover head is ready for its\ngate, it takes the slot ahead of every other head. Item 3 stays as\nit is, on your reasoning.\n\nNF-4. All four as you propose.\nQ1. Choose A. `Reads` moves to the client as a move, with no\n    change of behaviour, and the two client functions take a\n    reader port. There is one reader.\nQ2. An optional `admit` hook. MCP passes its tool policy. The\n    command line passes none, and the scope judges the install.\nQ3. A `send` port with the signature of `custody.send`.\nQ4. The client functions return typed refusals and do not throw\n    `Stop`. MCP maps each one to its present words, and tests fix\n    those words byte for byte. No error words move to the client.\n    The command line writes its own short lines. List each changed\n    command-line line in the note, old beside new, and change\n    docs/cli.md where it quotes one.\nOne options type carries the reader, the hook and the port for\nboth functions.\n\nQ-D1. The cutover deployment makes a new register on every\nWorker, the demo Worker included. The head carries no value that\nreads as a reference. Remove `DEMO_START_CONFIG` from\napps/room/wrangler.demo.jsonc. A demo Worker with no start config\nserves no start offer, demo-config.test.ts expects that, and the\nsmoke table expects 404 for the demo offer. After the deployment I\nmake the register and file a small configuration head with the\nnew reference. scripts/deploy.mjs refuses a changed checkout, so I\ncannot write a value in the deploy window.\n\nThe same question holds for every tracked value that names a room\nof the old format. Put one list in the note: each such value, its\nfile, and what the Worker does with it between the cutover\ndeployment and my configuration head. I expect at least\n`REGISTER_SCOPE` in each room configuration and `SCREEN_HOSTS` in\napps/sandbox/wrangler.rollout.jsonc, which names the Grow\ndirectory. I plan the deployment order from that list.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}